  {
    "@id": "http://purl.org/spar/tvc",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor": [
      {
        "@value": "David Shotton (https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5506-523X)"
      },
      {
        "@value": "Fabio Vitali (https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7562-5203)"
      },
      {
        "@value": "Sebastian Barzaghi (https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0799-1527)"
      }
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator": [
      {
        "@value": "Silvio Peroni (https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0530-4305)"
      }
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date": [
      {
        "@value": "2026-09-18"
      }
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\nThe **_Time-indexed Value in Context pattern (TVC)_** is an Ontology Design Pattern for the description of scenarios that involve entities having some value during a particular time and within a particular context.\n\n![The main architecture of TVC.](tvc.png)\n\nSometimes, we need to describe scenarios in which someone (e.g., a person) has a value (e.g., a particular role) during a particular time and for a particular context. \nFour different things are involved in these kinds of scenarios:\n\n1. the _entity_ having some value, e.g. a person or a document possessing a role or a status;\n\n2. the _value_ had by someone, e.g. a role or a status;\n\n3. the _time period_ during which the entity has that value, e.g. from April 2008 to September 2008;\n\n4. the particular _context_ that characterises the act of having that value, e.g. being a member of an institution or an editor of a particular journal.\n\nThought as a natural extension of the [_Time-indexed Situation pattern_](http://ontologydesignpatterns.org/wiki/Submissions:TimeIndexedSituation), TVC is able to describe these kinds of scenarios.\n\n## Examples of use\n\nIn the following subsections, we introduce some examples to showcase how to use TVC. \n\nThe prefixes that are used in all the examples provided below are defined as follows:\n\n        @prefix : <http://www.sparontologies.net/example/> .\n        @prefix tvc: <http://www.essepuntato.it/2012/04/tvc/> .\n        @prefix ti: <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/timeinterval.owl#> .\n        @prefix time: <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#> .\n        @prefix foaf: <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/> .\n        @prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n\n### Holding a role within a specific time frame\n\nTVC easily allows one to model people's roles within certain contexts (e.g., organisations) and how these change through time, while keeping track of the fact that they all refer to the same entities.\n\nThe following example shows how to model the fact that a researcher holds the role of editor-in-chief for a scientific journal for a specific time interval.\n\n        :john-doe a foaf:Person ;\n            tvc:hasValue :editorial-role-situation .\n\n        :editorial-role-situation a tvc:ValueInTime ;\n            tvc:withValue :editor-in-chief ;\n            tvc:withinContext :journal-of-semantics ;\n            tvc:atTime :tenure-interval .\n\n        :tenure-interval a ti:TimeInterval ;\n            ti:hasIntervalStartDate \"2020-01-01\"^^xsd:date ;\n            ti:hasIntervalEndDate \"2024-12-31\"^^xsd:date .\n\n        :journal-of-semantics a foaf:Organization .\n\n## Competency Questions\n\nTVC can be used for answering several questions related to values that change in time, according to some context.\n\nIn the following subsections, some of them are introduced together with their respective SPARQL queries. \n\nThe prefixes that are used in all the SPARQL queries provided below are defined as follows:\n\n        PREFIX : <http://www.sparontologies.net/example/>\n        PREFIX tvc: <http://www.essepuntato.it/2012/04/tvc/>\n        PREFIX ti: <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/timeinterval.owl#>\n\n### CQ1\n\nWhat value did a specific entity hold, within which context, and during what time interval?\n        \n        SELECT ?value ?context ?startDate ?endDate WHERE {\n            :john-doe tvc:hasValue ?sit .\n            ?sit tvc:withValue ?value ;\n                 tvc:withinContext ?context ;\n                 tvc:atTime ?interval .\n            OPTIONAL { ?interval ti:hasIntervalStartDate ?startDate . }\n            OPTIONAL { ?interval ti:hasIntervalEndDate ?endDate . }\n        }\n\n### CQ2\n\nWhich entities held a specific value within a given context?\n\n        SELECT ?entity ?sit WHERE {\n            ?entity tvc:hasValue ?sit .\n            ?sit tvc:withValue :editor-in-chief ;\n                tvc:withinContext :journal-of-semantics .\n        }\n\n"
      }
    ],
